c-world-of-darkness/1067484-was-the-current-xp-rating-debate-ever-settled?p=1067986#post1067986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">glad to see i wasn't doing it wrong all the time.. still isn't it a bit wierd that the first dot of an ability costs more than the second? or is slightly improving something a little easier once you learn the ropes?</div> </div> </div> </div>You must unlearn what you think you know grasshopper!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T10:24:09-07:00","id":1068037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067484-was-the-current-xp-rating-debate-ever-settled?p=1067986#post1067986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">glad to see i wasn't doing it wrong all the time.. still isn't it a bit wierd that the first dot of an ability costs more than the second? or is slightly improving something a little easier once you learn the ropes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it represents reality pretty well. Learning something new is harder than expanding your skills while already knowing the basics. After you're at a certain level it becomes harder again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T14:01:12-07:00","id":1068088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067484-was-the-current-xp-rating-debate-ever-settled?p=1067986#post1067986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">glad to see i wasn't doing it wrong all the time.. still isn't it a bit wierd that the first dot of an ability costs more than the second?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's weird.<br /> <br /> 1) It doesn't actually model anything important from the sense of verisimilitude. The distance between dots in the games' description abstract out too far for any sort of comparison to real world experiences. There's some validity (though it doesn't actually apply to all human learning, which is too complex for a game to really model anyway) to the feeling of a &quot;dip&quot; in difficulty of progress that comes out of the lecture based Western education model, but it's something that doesn't bear out when on the abstract scale of the traits in the game. Knowledges are the easiest way to demonstrate this, because they have the most direct comparison to real world learning. Academics 1 is supposed to represent the equivalent of a high school education, while Academics 2 is supposed to represent the equivalent of a college/university education. That's too pulled back for the &quot;dip&quot; to make sense, because that's saying college is easier than high-school, not the experience of 100 and 200 level college courses feeling harder than 200 and 300 level courses due to the hump of mastering new concepts before courses that focus on applying those concepts (as well as the adjustment to a college setting).<br /> <br /> 2) It creates weird mechanical incentives. With Linear Creation/Quadratic Advancement, what's the most BP/XP efficient ways to build a character get screwy and are not always intuitive. For example with Abilities you want to either take 1 or 3 in a trait you plan to invest in over time. Disciplines though, give you the best pay off if you spread out with 1s instead. While you can't get rid of the LCQA issues completely by getting rid of the weird &quot;dip&quot; the way the WoD handles XP, it doesn't actually help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T02:02:12-07:00","id":1068223,"title":"","content":"Remove Freebies, except for Merits/Flaws and Backgrounds. Then give each PC an amount of EXP to use equivalent to the age of the concept and the game's power level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T02:51:57-07:00","id":1068227,"title":"","content":"Fixing the LCQA issue is not complicated (in either direction, the CofD went the other way and just had everything go off linear costs so that char-gen XP is easier to handle), but it creates a system environment where there &quot;dip&quot; creates mechanical oddities that take considerable system mastery to understand and navigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T10:31:22-07:00","id":1068738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067484-was-the-current-xp-rating-debate-ever-settled?p=1067986#post1067986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">glad to see i wasn't doing it wrong all the time.. still isn't it a bit wierd that the first dot of an ability costs more than the second? or is slightly improving something a little easier once you learn the ropes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first dot represents a 2-die swing as you lose the untrained penalty and then add a die to the pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T17:14:22-07:00","id":1068942,"title":"","content":"Erm, the first dot in the WoD (as opposed to the CofD) doesn't really play out like that because the &quot;untrained&quot; penalty is highly variable.<br /> <br /> Talents offer no untrained penalty, so the first dot doesn't do anything more than +1 to your pool. Skills have a +1 difficulty untrained penalty which is very hard to nail down the exact value of, but generally not worth the same as +1 die (while perhaps a Merit that's too cheap, Ability Aptitude is usual a 1 dot Merit which means -2 difficulty is worth half the cost of an Ability dot in freebie costs). Knowledges don't even allow a roll, which is is anywhere from a +2 to +6 die swing for mortal level characters depending on their Attributes.<br /> <br /> Most other traits are either automatic minimum of 1, or like Knowledges you don't get to roll without having dots (like pretty much all powers).<br /> <br /> This is, again, an issue with the oddities this creates in what the best investments are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T08:36:50-07:00","id":1069375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067484-was-the-current-xp-rating-debate-ever-settled?p=1068942#post1068942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm, the first dot in the WoD (as opposed to the CofD) doesn't really play out like that because the &quot;untrained&quot; penalty is highly variable.<br /> <br /> Talents offer no untrained penalty, so the first dot doesn't do anything more than +1 to your pool. Skills have a +1 difficulty untrained penalty which is very hard to nail down the exact value of, but generally not worth the same as +1 die (while perhaps a Merit that's too cheap, Ability Aptitude is usual a 1 dot Merit which means -2 difficulty is worth half the cost of an Ability dot in freebie costs). Knowledges don't even allow a roll, which is is anywhere from a +2 to +6 die swing for mortal level characters depending on their Attributes.<br /> <br /> Most other traits are either automatic minimum of 1, or like Knowledges you don't get to roll without having dots (like pretty much all powers).<br /> <br /> This is, again, an issue with the oddities this creates in what the best investments are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> of course &quot;best investments&quot; is by itsself subjective. for instance,melee,brawl,athletics,firears,intimidatio n is all that munchkins care about,regarding knowledges as wasted points<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:17:24-07:00","id":1069615,"title":"","content":"I meant in a purely mechanical sense.<br /> <br /> That said, the WoD system is actually designed to facilitate non-combat &quot;munchkins&quot; or whatever; especially since Knowledges can't even be rolled if you don't have them. I've seen countless PvP oriented VtM games quickly devolve into the politics &quot;munchkins&quot; making the combat focused characters irrelevant because the politics/social oriented PCs only need enough combat ability to run away (which doesn't take that much) any fair fights, and then use all their traits to turn the Prince/Primogen/etc. against the combat characters that step out of line and have the Sheriff and/or Scourge and so on to take care of combat for them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}